;; tags: mem-ops, addressing
;; expect: 4242
;; Large base+offset addressing. The byte offset (16 * 8 == 128) still
;; encodes directly as LDR Xt, [Xn, #128] (uimm12 scaled by 8 covers up
;; to 32760). On x86 this remains a single MOV r64, [reg + disp32].
;; This is the regression check that the codegen actually scales the
;; immediate by the access size and picks the correct addressing mode
;; rather than naively shoving the byte offset in.
(defun main ()
  (let ((buf (new 'stack-no-clear 'array int64 17)))
    (set! (-> buf 16) 4242)
    (format #t "~D~%" (-> buf 16))))
